Restore declarations for the Windows-only methods on
ClientSharedImageInterface and GpuChannelSharedImageInterface so that the
definitions enabled by 0021 actually have matching declarations under MinGW.

0017-chromium-mingw-link-fixes.patch wrapped these declarations in
BUILDFLAG(IS_MSVC) (in addition to the outer BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) for the
ClientSharedImageInterface ones). With 0021 reverting the IS_MSVC sites in
the corresponding .cc files back to IS_WIN, the .cc files now define methods
whose declarations are still gated out under MinGW. Build error:

  client_shared_image_interface.cc:231:6: error: no declaration matches
    'void gpu::ClientSharedImageInterface::CopyToGpuMemoryBufferAsync(...)'

(plus four siblings: UpdateSharedImage(D3DSharedFence), CopyNativeGmbToShared
MemorySync/Async, IsConnected.)

Three sites:
  * gpu/ipc/client/client_shared_image_interface.h: drop the inner
    `#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MSVC)` / `#endif // BUILDFLAG(IS_MSVC)` so the
    declarations live inside the outer `#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)` block.
  * gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel_shared_image_interface.h: revert
    BUILDFLAG(IS_MSVC) -> BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) for CreateSharedImageForD3D11Video.
  * gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel_shared_image_interface.cc: same revert at the
    matching definition.

These mirror the pattern already done by 0021 for the other shared-image
interface files.

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/ipc/client/client_shared_image_interface.h b/src/3rdparty/chromium/gpu/ipc/client/client_shared_image_interface.h
